              "path": "docs/specs/b1/tasks/01_validate.md",
              "heading": "Technical proposal",
              "text": "## Technical proposal\n\nProposal B1-P1-parse implements B1-001, B1-002, the empty validate case of B1-003, and B1-004. Proposed binding module records.mjs exports parseRecords(text): Array<{id: string, amount: number}>. It is pure, owns a fresh per-call duplicate-ID Set and output array, and returns only after the entire input passes. It throws on invalid input without exposing partial records. No process, filesystem or output dependency enters this module.\n\nThe parser accepts empty text, otherwise splits on LF and removes at most one trailing empty element. Each remaining row must have exactly two comma-separated fields: an ID matching the entire ASCII [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ pattern and an amount matching entire ASCII [0-9]+ whose Number conversion is a nonnegative safe integer. IDs remain case-sensitive, input order is preserved, whitespace and CR are not trimmed, and duplicate IDs are rejected. Leading zeroes are valid decimal digits.\n\ncli.mjs owns dispatch, synchronous file-byte reads and fatal UTF-8 decoding with BOM preserved for validation rather than silently stripped. validate calls parseRecords exactly once, serializes the completed array with JSON.stringify, then writes one newline-terminated result. Input read/decode/validation failures map to exit 2, empty stdout and INVALID_INPUT followed by LF on stderr. No stdout is written before all validation completes. Existing help text and unknown-command behavior remain exact. Do not add dependencies or implement summarize in this packet. Internal helper names and equivalent statement organization remain flexible; parseRecords signature and module boundary are binding because packet B1-P2 consumes them.\n\nKeep test-process.mjs and package.json's existing test command unchanged. CLI checks use its real runCli(args, { env }) subprocess capture, including exact stdout/stderr, status and signal assertions. Preserve unrelated.txt exactly. Production ownership is cli.mjs and new records.mjs only; test additions belong in test.mjs.\n\n",
              "digest": "7bda6a5a71bc1ff1ca8da9cdbd6b618efa4ef57b10fbdf9c5fb45d253b676041"
            }
