              "path": "docs/specs/b1/tasks/02_summarize.md",
              "heading": "Technical proposal",
              "text": "## Technical proposal\n\nProposal B1-P2-bigint implements B1-002, B1-003, B1-004 and B1-005, after B1-P1. cli.mjs reads and decodes the entire file through the B1-P1 input path and calls records.mjs parseRecords(text): Array<{id: string, amount: number}> once. It must consume that same validator, with no duplicate row parser. The authoritative shared contract is tasks/01_validate.md, Technical proposal, bound as an additional source to this proposal. The parser is independent of the CLI; summarize depends on it.\n\nProposed private summarizeRecords(records) computes count from array length and total by adding BigInt(record.amount) into an initial 0n. This function name is illustrative; exact accumulation and separation from input validation are binding. Validated safe integers convert exactly. Serialize a fixed JSON object shape with count and total fields, emitting the BigInt total's base-10 digits directly as an unquoted JSON integer token, with a terminating LF. Never convert the accumulated total to Number or serialize it as a quoted string. Empty records yield {\"count\":0,\"total\":0}. The two amounts 9007199254740991 and 2 yield {\"count\":2,\"total\":9007199254740993}. BigInt is internal only; validate retains numeric safe-integer amounts.\n\nValidation completes before aggregation/output; read, decode and validation failures retain exit 2, empty stdout and INVALID_INPUT followed by LF on stderr. All per-invocation state is local and discarded on exit. Preserve help, unknown commands, validate and test infrastructure. Production ownership is cli.mjs only; test additions belong in test.mjs, using real runCli subprocess assertions with exact streams/status/signal. No dependencies or changes to unrelated.txt. A viable alternative is decimal-string addition, but BigInt is recommended for less arithmetic code and simpler verification.\n\n",
